# Images go through Git LFS rather than being stored as plain blobs, so `web/`'s assets are
# pointers and the bytes stay out of the packfile every clone downloads. A blob committed
# without this stays in history at full size even after the file is deleted, and only a
# history rewrite gets it back out. Audio is not listed here because it does not belong in
# the repository at all; see .gitignore.
*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpeg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.webp filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
